virglrenderer: copy clip distances 4..7 the guest's Mesa leaves in a temp (#692)

What: after a MOV OUT[clip 0..3], TEMP[X] with an identity swizzle and no
modifiers, where TEMP[X] is a temp the shader indexes at run time without an
ARRAY declaration (virgl-shader-indirect-temps.patch makes it an array), the
GLSL also sets clip_dist_temp[1] from TEMP[X+1] (clip_dist_temp[1] =
vec4(temp18[1]);). Only when the shader declares more than 4 clip distances,
TEMP[X+1] is in the same array, and the shader never writes the second clip
distance register itself, directly or with an index (the first pass notes
that). Any other shader gets the same GLSL as before; every stage the same.
Why: the guest's Mesa (virgl_tgsi.c, the same in Mesa 26.2.5, 26.2.6 and main)
writes the two clip distance outputs through two temps, TEMP[18..19]. A write
in a loop goes to TEMP[ADDR+18], and the copy after it is always MOV OUT[1],
TEMP[18], so distances 4..7 never reached OUT[2] and gl_ClipDistance[4..7] was
undefined: on the M4 a negative distance 5 did not clip (tcs-8loop-clip5,
tcs-8wloop-clip5 on a new Omarchy 4.5 VM), on the M1 Max the looped forms drew
nothing (tcs-8*loop-keep). OmacVM's guest Mesa fix (#694) also copies TEMP[19]
but reaches no VM; this sends vrend the same copy for every 4.0 and 4.5 VM. A
shader that copies OUT[2] itself (#694's Mesa, a fixed upstream Mesa) is left
as it is.
Upstream: not sent (works around a Mesa virgl driver bug; the fix belongs in
Mesa's virgl_tgsi.c).
Test: Tests/virgl/test-core-glsl-shaders.c: the guest's own TCS loop with 8
distances and the loop forms with 5 to 8 distances (TCS, VS, GS, TES, whole and
separable) have the copy and compile on the Mac's GL; 1 to 4 distances, the
forms that copy OUT[2] themselves, a distance 5 written after the loop and
clip outputs written as one indexed array have none. VM rows: tclip692 on
Omarchy 4.5.
